<title>FRANCE: ADP-New York top ex-Paris cargo destination Jan-Feb.</title>
<headline>ADP-New York top ex-Paris cargo destination Jan-Feb.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top export destination from Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in the first two months of 1997.</p>
<p>The top ten ex-Paris air cargo destinations in January-February 1997, with the percentage change against the same period 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>			  Jan-Feb  pct change</p>
<p> 1  New York	   5,255   up    0.4</p>
<p> 2  Chicago	    4,228   up   16.7</p>
<p> 3  Tokyo		3,843   down 18.4</p>
<p> 4  Hong Kong	  3,133   down  1.3</p>
<p> 5  Sao Paulo	  2,266   up   70.9</p>
<p> 6  Montreal	   2,117   down 11.4</p>
<p> 7  Mexico City	2,002   up    7.8</p>
<p> 8  Singapore	  1,750   up   46.5</p>
<p> 9  Los Angeles	1,582   down 11.8</p>
<p> 10 Dubai		1,323   down  2.4</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
